WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.502
-This feels like a rehearsal.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.071
-Yeah. But if anything's good,
we'll keep it.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.306
-Great.
-Because you're actually --

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:10.643
You are doing a show every night
in a theater with human beings.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.346
-I am. And, by the way,
is everybody here vaccinated?

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.514
-Yeah.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.150
-Not me. Let me tell you why.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.718
Seth, there's a lot of
information out there.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.220
I felt like tonight's the night

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.723
I'm going to right
a lot of wrongs.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.158
Go ahead.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:29.695
-How is it doing shows
for people wearing masks?

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:34.467
-I thought it would bother me,
and then I remembered that

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.870
I got my start in comedy
doing stand-up

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.239
at "Eyes Wide Shut"-style
sex parties.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.942
-Oh, right, I forgot about that.
So it was almost all masks.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.344
-Yeah. That was all masks.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.045
-And you were like an opener,
right?

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.847
You'd come on
before the sex started?

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:51.884
-I would kind of
get them in the mood.

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:53.519
Couple sex jokes.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.188
-'Cause I've always heard
the worst thing

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.790
was, like, comedians in the '70s
would open for,

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.626
like, rock acts a lot,
like before concerts.

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.094
-Edgar Winter.

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:04.964
But yeah, they didn't do "Eyes
Wide Shut"-style sex parties.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.732
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.701
-I feel like the stakes there --
'Cause I feel like people

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.503
are like, "Let's get this guy
off stage."

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:14.007
-And to all of my old friends
watching, fidelio.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.642
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.411
Fidelio.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.079
-Is that your safe word?

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:24.684
-No, fidelio is the password

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.119
that Tom Cruise says
to get into the party.

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.821
-Really?
-And all the freaks

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:31.190
in the studio
who laughed at that

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.759
have watched the movie
multiple times.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.627
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.696
And now they know.
-But just that part.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:40.833
-Yeah, that's all.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:46.205
Hey, so, "3 Mics," one of
the best stand-up specials

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.041
of the last I'm going to say
20 years.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.508
-Damn!

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:52.077
-One of the mikes was about
emotional stuff,

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:57.016
and this show strikes me
as an extension of that.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:00.018
-It is somewhat of an extension.

00:02:00.018 --> 00:02:03.022
It's less delineated.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.291
Like, "3 Mics" was like
I'm gonna be funny

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.726
and everybody would be like,
"Alright, he's gonna be funny."

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.495
And then I'd be like,
"Alright, I'm gonna be sad."

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:11.497
And everybody would be sad
and then I'd do one-liners

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:13.532
and they'd be whatever they are
for the one-liners.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:16.569
This is more interwoven.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:20.806
It's a bit like I start off kind
of like a glib comedian, right?

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:25.978
And slowly but surely I show
that I'm a human boy inside.

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:29.248
[ Laughter ]
-You are a human boy inside.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.516
One of the things
you talk about --

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.685
and you and I are the same age.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.887
We're both comedians.
One difference between us

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.923
is I am married,
I have children.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:40.826
-Income.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:45.631
-Which I really asked not to
make tonight about but...

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:47.333
But you --
-Seriously, what do you make?

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.503
-You know who actually asked me
that once?

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.204
-This is my favorite story
and I think about him

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:53.940
every time I say it --
every time I see him.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.576
Tell the story.
-I did a talk show.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.411
There was someone who had
a short-lived talk show.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.578
I was a guest on it, and they,

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:01.847
on air, asked me
how much I make.

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:04.117
And that person was...?
-John McEnroe.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.118
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:08.521
The weirdest part is that
John McEnroe had a talk show.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.588
-He did.
-Yeah.

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.156
-And it was filmed in Secaucus.

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:12.391
I had to go to New Jersey.

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:14.160
-Yeah. Did you know
you were doing a talk show

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.396
or you just got kidnapped?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.431
-A guy in a van said,
"You like tennis?"

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:23.802
[ Laughter ]
-"Who doesn't like tennis? Hey!"

00:03:23.802 --> 00:03:26.673
-So, someone drew you.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:32.678
-I was on Joe Rogan's podcast,
which never makes the news.

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:34.881
He does a small podcast.
-He does a small podcast, yeah.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.849
-So I was on
Joe Rogan's podcast.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.385
Apparently there's a guy
who draws the guest

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.687
while they're on, right?
-Yeah.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:44.524
-So this is a --
He made a drawing of me.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.226
-Uh-huh.
-And I thought it was so stupid.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.427
Will you show the drawing,
please?

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:50.596
-I'm going to start
by showing the drawing.

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:52.865
I want to cover up --
Alright, that's the drawing.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.167
-I mean, you want to
talk about ghoulish.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:58.604
-Yeah, that's not -- I really
like the poster for your show.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.439
I think it shows
how you're a handsome person.

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.374
This is deeply unfair.
-This is the opposite.

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:04.043
This is how I feel.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.811
[ Laughter ]
-Aww.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.315
That's what you can see
in the show, stuff like this.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.817
-I feel like
you'll blow this up.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.018
We're shooting in 4K.
Do a little tighter.

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:14.320
[ Laughter ]
-Alright. So wait.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.689
Now tell me how you --
-I was like, "You know what?

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:20.393
That's a bad picture, but I'd be
a sucker not to pose like that

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.761
on my driver's license photo."

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.096
-So you went and posed for
your driver's license photo

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.932
hoping to emulate that.
-To capture what it was.

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.734
And I think I did it.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:32.638
Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:34.006
Wow!

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:37.676
-I mean, it is --
there's no way --

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:39.712
There's no way,
if a cop asks for your license

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.447
and you give him that,
you get away with a warning.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:44.850
-I think you're getting away
with everything or nothing.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.686
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:53.425
You talk about dating models.

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:55.561
-I guess I've dated
a few models.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.197
-Yeah.
-You know, Seth, ultimately

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.600
what I learned was
that dating a model

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.436
is like owning a dune buggy.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:05.771
And dating a model is
like owning a dune buggy

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:09.141
because at the beach it's great,
but every everywhere else,

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.943
you're like, "I shouldn't have
brought you here."

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:15.915
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.951
Guys, that's probably
the best joke in my show.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:19.985
-And you gave it away.

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:23.723
-And I gave it away for $460.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.324
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:26.892
-Before taxes.
-Before taxes.

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:29.395
-Before your agent took a bite.
-Yes.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.731
[ Laughter ]
And you make the same, right?

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:32.998
$467?

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:37.670
-Yeah, but my agents don't
commission Tuesdays.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.338
So I make a little bit more.
-Oh, that's really cool.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.140
-Hey, so, you kind of
have a dune buggy.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.308
-This is a lot of --

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.843
-This is the dumbest thing
I've ever seen.

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:50.516
-Okay, so, I -- Sometimes I'll
work with comedians on their --

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:54.820
I directed your Netflix special,
"Lobby Baby," of course.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.322
Would have gotten
a round of applause.

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.490
-Yeah, would've I think
on a normal day.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:01.226
-I think at least
a hearty six-seconder

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:02.461
if not a standing ovation.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:04.429
-Yeah.
The crew, on the other hand.

00:06:04.429 --> 00:06:06.833
-The crew, on the other hand.
-Could not move a muscle.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:09.202
-They are checking
their phones right now.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:11.503
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:18.544
And so I will -- So, I helped
Chris Rock on his last Netflix,

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:21.147
and he gave me money, right?

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:23.482
A nice, fine amount of money,
right?

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.984
And then -- $467.

00:06:25.984 --> 00:06:30.622
And then his assistant
kept calling me,

00:06:30.622 --> 00:06:32.057
"when are you going to be home,
when are you going to be home,

00:06:32.057 --> 00:06:33.059
when are you going to be home."

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.493
I'm like,
"Something good's coming."

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:36.028
Didn't know what
it was going to be.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:42.735
And I go outside and he got me
this, like, Batmobile thing.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:46.738
It's a three-wheel motorcycle,
and the guy's like,

00:06:46.738 --> 00:06:49.175
"Alright, sign for it."
And I go, "I don't want it."

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:51.610
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.512
And he's like, "No, but you got
to sign for it."

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:56.549
I'm like,
"No. I'm not taking it."

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.183
And he's like, "I'll bring it
into your garage."

00:06:58.183 --> 00:07:01.354
I go, "If it goes into my
garage, I'll never get rid of it

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:02.822
so I will not sign for it."

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:04.423
And the guy thought
I was doing a bit.

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:08.027
And then eventually I just said,
"Hey, man,

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.662
I'm never taking this.
What do we do?"

00:07:10.662 --> 00:07:12.832
So the guy is like,

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:16.535
"We'll sell it on layaway
at the dealership."

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:19.371
So I'm like,
"I'm going to make $27,000

00:07:19.371 --> 00:07:21.741
off this goofy-ass motorcycle."

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.476
This is such a goofy motorcycle,

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:26.145
there is a button
that says "traction."

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:30.182
So I got to hit
a button for traction? Okay.

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:35.288
So I call the car dealership
a few weeks later,

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:36.588
and they're giving me
the runaround.

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:37.990
And eventually he goes,
"Oh, they didn't tell you?

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.725
They gave it to somebody else."

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:43.829
So I think what Rock did
was I don't -- I may be wrong,

00:07:43.829 --> 00:07:45.731
but I believe he gave it to

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:49.001
the roast master general
Jeff Ross as a gift.

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:52.605
-So keep an eye out if you see
one of those three-wheelers.

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:54.874
-Jeff used it.
It found a good home.

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.075
-Alright.

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:57.710
-And Rock goes, "Well, no,
I just thought --"

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.444
I go, "Why would you get me
a motorcycle?"

00:07:59.444 --> 00:08:00.913
He's like, "I don't know.
I just thought like --"

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:03.515
Jay Leno goes out with him
sometimes.

00:08:03.515 --> 00:08:06.051
I'm like, "So you think
what would Neal want?

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:07.553
Well, what does Jay Leno want?"

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.755
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.623
-I'd like to close,
as we always do,

00:08:11.623 --> 00:08:14.626
with a photo that was taken
of us back in the day.

00:08:14.626 --> 00:08:17.430
-This was 2005.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.232
-2005, you and I went out
a fair amount.

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:22.034
We went out to social occasions

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:23.802
where people danced on
banquettes

00:08:23.802 --> 00:08:26.772
and drank Dutch beer,
as I'm doing in this photo.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.041
And you feel like this photo --

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.610
-This is why you're married

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.812
and I'm doing a show
called "Unacceptable"

00:08:33.812 --> 00:08:37.049
at the Cherry Lane Theatre,
unacceptableshow.com.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:40.920
This is the difference
between Seth and Neal,

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.056
why Seth is married
and Neal is still single.

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:45.891
-Two gentlemen of the same age
with similar faces.

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:49.261
-We're gonna start
tight on Seth.

00:08:49.261 --> 00:08:51.297
And then go to Seth.

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:54.433
And then wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:59.638
Neal's got that thousand-yard
stare, thinking of

00:08:59.638 --> 00:09:03.409
"Eyes Wide Shut"-style
sex parties gone awry.

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.611
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:06.912
-Buddy, it's always great
to have you here.

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:09.115
-Buddy, I love you.
-I love you too.

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:13.552
-I'm so happy that I get to
touch your shoulder.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.621
-Congrats on the show.
The show is great.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.022
I'm really happy you're doing it
and that you're going to be

00:09:17.022 --> 00:09:19.124
in the city till November.
Neal Brennan, "Unacceptable."

00:09:19.124 --> 00:09:21.193
It's playing at the Cherry Lane
through November 21st.

